# Vercel serves the committed repo root as static files — there is no build
# command — so anything left in the deployment is publicly fetchable at the
# site's domain. Only the generated output belongs there.
#
# Verify after changing this: /MIGRATION.md must 404 while /, /sitemap.xml,
# /llms.txt, /robots.txt and /assets/css/main.css still resolve.

# Page sources, the builder, and the dead Dropbox-era deploy script.
# The finished pages are committed at the repo root; these are how they're made.
_src/

# Internal tooling — the preflight gate.
_dev/

# Internal documentation. MIGRATION.md is the reason this file exists: it
# carries the client's ad spend, their Search Console history and the owner's
# own words about the business. None of that should ever be reachable at
# jupiterlaser.com/MIGRATION.md.
#
# Public text files are .txt/.xml (llms.txt, robots.txt, sitemap.xml) and are
# unaffected by this rule.
*.md

# Portability files for other hosts. Inert on Vercel, which reads vercel.json.
_redirects
.htaccess

# OS and editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
